Subject: [PATCH] ImGui SDL_GPU backend: force enable_depth_clip = true

FNA3D creates its SDL_GPUDevice with the Vulkan depthClamp feature explicitly
disabled (see FNA3D_Driver_SDL.c: SDL.gpu.device.create.feature.depth_clamping
= false, for portability to older/mobile devices). Per SDL's docs, when
depth_clamping is disabled the device has no depth-clamp support and
SDL_GPURasterizerState.enable_depth_clip must ALWAYS be true; otherwise
SDL_CreateGPUGraphicsPipeline asserts:

    Rasterizer state enable_depth_clip must be set to true
    (FEATURE_DEPTH_CLAMPING disabled)

The vendored imgui_impl_sdlgpu3 backend hardcodes enable_depth_clip = false
(i.e. "use depth clamp"), which is only valid on a device that kept depthClamp
enabled. That trips the assertion on every FNA3D device. Depth clip vs clamp is
irrelevant to ImGui's 2D geometry (rendered with the depth test off), so forcing
true is correct and portable.

This lives as a tracked patch (applied at configure time by CMake) so the fix
survives `git submodule update` without carrying a fork of the imgui submodule.

diff --git a/backends/imgui_impl_sdlgpu3.cpp b/backends/imgui_impl_sdlgpu3.cpp
index 8f0408c82..ba6772b12 100644
--- a/backends/imgui_impl_sdlgpu3.cpp
+++ b/backends/imgui_impl_sdlgpu3.cpp
@@ -538,8 +538,8 @@ static void ImGui_ImplSDLGPU3_CreateGraphicsPipeline()
     rasterizer_state.fill_mode = SDL_GPU_FILLMODE_FILL;
     rasterizer_state.cull_mode = SDL_GPU_CULLMODE_NONE;
     rasterizer_state.front_face = SDL_GPU_FRONTFACE_COUNTER_CLOCKWISE;
     rasterizer_state.enable_depth_bias = false;
-    rasterizer_state.enable_depth_clip = false;
+    rasterizer_state.enable_depth_clip = true;
 
     SDL_GPUMultisampleState multisample_state = {};
     multisample_state.sample_count = v->MSAASamples;
